{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:Observations.DiagrammaticDoubleMagicLrFusion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"Observations.DiagrammaticDoubleMagicLrFusion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Common.MagicNumbers"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.nu_selfConjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.nu_selfConjugate","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L191-L210","doc":"**Self-conjugacy of the fused partition is preserved by the LR rigidity**\n— and now this docstring is true.\n\nUntil 2026-09-03 the body was `c.nuZN_selfConj`, a field of the class, so\nnothing was preserved by anything; the sentence above and the body\ndisagreed.\n\nThe derivation: LR conjugation symmetry gives\n`c^{ν'}_{λ' μ'} = c^ν_{λ μ}`, and `λ' = λ`, `μ' = μ` by the two\nsaturated-shell hypotheses, so `c^{ν'}_{λ μ} = c^{ν}_{λ μ} = 1 ≠ 0`. LR\nrigidity off the fused partition then forces `ν' = ν_{ZN}` — which is\nself-conjugacy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.lr_kronecker","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.lr_kronecker","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L180-L189","doc":"Stronger biconditional: under the conjecture, the LR\ncoefficient at any `ν` is exactly `1` if `ν = ν_{ZN}` and `0`\notherwise. The two cases together fully characterise the LR\nproduct as a Kronecker delta. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.nu_iff_lr_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.nu_iff_lr_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L166-L177","doc":"Biconditional characterisation of `ν_{ZN}`: under the\nconjecture, `ν` equals the fused partition iff the LR\ncoefficient is non-zero (equivalently, equal to 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.nu_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.nu_unique","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L155-L164","doc":"Conditional theorem: under the double-magic conjecture, the\nfused partition `ν_{ZN}` is the unique partition with non-zero\nLR coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.lr_concentrated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.lr_concentrated","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L143-L153","doc":"Conditional theorem: under the double-magic conjecture, the LR\nproduct is concentrated at the unique fused self-conjugate\npartition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.lr_vanishes_off","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.lr_vanishes_off","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L140-L140","doc":"LR-rigidity off the fused partition: multiplicity zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.lr_unique_at_nu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.lr_unique_at_nu","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L138-L138","doc":"LR-rigidity at the fused partition: multiplicity one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.nuZN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.nuZN","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L132-L132","doc":"The unique fused partition at level `Z + N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.muN_selfConj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.muN_selfConj","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L130-L130","doc":"It is self-conjugate, `μ' = μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.muN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.muN","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L128-L128","doc":"The unique saturated-shell partition at level `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.lambdaZ_selfConj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.lambdaZ_selfConj","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L126-L126","doc":"It is self-conjugate, `λ' = λ`.  Written as the equation rather than\nvia `LRFusionData.SelfConjugate`, which needs a `LRFusionData` term this\nclass body does not yet have; the two are definitionally equal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.lambdaZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.lambdaZ","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L122-L122","doc":"The unique saturated-shell partition at level `Z` (provided by\nthe categorical-neutrality conjecture upstream). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.doubleMagic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.doubleMagic","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L119-L119","doc":"Precondition: both `Z` and `N` are magic numbers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.mk","kind":"ctor","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L117-L117","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.toLRFusionData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture.toLRFusionData","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L117-L140","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagicConjecture","kind":"class","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L109-L140","doc":"The conjecture, encoded as a class.\n\nA `DoubleMagicConjecture Z N` instance asserts that, when both\n`Z` and `N` are saturated and the unique saturated-shell\npartition at each level is self-conjugate, the LR product\ncollapses to a unique self-conjugate fused partition with\nmultiplicity one. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion","label":"conj:diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData.SelfConjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData.SelfConjugate","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L99-L107","doc":"**Self-conjugacy**, `λ' = λ`.\n\nA *definition* over `conj`, not a free predicate field. As a field an\ninstance could take `SelfConjugate := fun _ => True` and discharge every\nself-conjugacy hypothesis of the conjecture with `trivial`; here the\nhypotheses constrain the partition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData.lr_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData.lr_conj","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L96-L96","doc":"**LR conjugation symmetry**, `c^ν_{λ μ} = c^{ν'}_{λ' μ'}`.\n\nA theorem of Littlewood–Richardson theory, not part of the conjecture:\nit holds for the actual LR coefficients and is recorded here because\nthis carrier abstracts them. It is what makes `nu_selfConjugate`\nderivable instead of assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData.lr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData.lr","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L88-L88","doc":"The LR coefficient `c^ν_{λ μ}` as a natural number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData.Specht","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData.Specht","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L86-L86","doc":"The Specht module attached to a partition (abstract carrier). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData.conj_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData.conj_conj","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L84-L84","doc":"Conjugation is an involution, `λ'' = λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData.conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData.conj","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L82-L82","doc":"Conjugation (transpose) of a Young diagram, `λ ↦ λ'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData.Partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData.Partition","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L80-L80","doc":"Abstract carrier for partitions of a given size. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.LRFusionData","kind":"class","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L71-L97","doc":"Abstract data of an LR-fusion outcome at level `Z + N`.\n\nConcretely the QOU substrate instantiates `Specht λ` as the\n`H_{|λ|}(q)`-module structure on the Specht module of the\npartition `λ`, and `lrFusion λ μ ν` records the LR-coefficient\n`c^ν_{λ μ}`. The conjecture below asks for collapse to a unique\n`ν` with multiplicity one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.DoubleMagic","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L68-L69","doc":"Both `Z` and `N` are saturated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LRFusion.magicSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LRFusion.magicSet","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0}]}